{
  "fixture_version": 3,
  "purpose": "Neutral public-wire fixture for rpc_v0.3: the JSON objects a node returns from get_block_by_height and accepts in submit_transaction once TransactionPayload::ComputeTask exists. Pins the minimal, canonical and maximal ComputeTask transaction objects, a block carrying all three payload variants, the observed behaviour of the published rpc_v0.2 SDK, and the unknown-variant rule. Version 2 (RFC 0006 section 2, S1-5): every transaction signature is over \"mbongo-tx:v2\" || chain_id || the transaction fields, for the dev chain below. The fields, encodings of tasks and receipts, and receipt signatures are those of version 1. Version 3 (RFC 0006 section 3 and section 7, S1-7): a block result carries header.producer and producer_signature.",
  "supersedes": "test-vectors/rpc/compute-task-rpc-v2.json",
  "chain": {
    "chain_id": "2fd700acc09b3d1752ca6fe21e7d6f4844917c5a9fcd41a34fe1d13d7deed1a4",
    "chain_id_source": "crates/mbongo-core/genesis/dev.json, the dev genesis: chain_id = BLAKE3(\"mbongo:chain-id:v1\" || file_bytes)",
    "signing_domain": {
      "ascii": "mbongo-tx:v2",
      "hex": "6d626f6e676f2d74783a7632",
      "length": 12
    },
    "other_chain_id": "5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a5a",
    "other_chain_id_use": "no signature in this file verifies for it: a signature for one network does not verify on another"
  },
  "authority": {
    "rpc_contract": "docs/specs/rpc_v0.3.md §1 (byte encoding), §4.1 (payload union), §4.4 (ComputeTask object)",
    "frozen_predecessor": "docs/specs/rpc_v0.2.md — unchanged; its §4.1 payload union is what v0.3 widens",
    "protocol_bytes": "test-vectors/compute-task/compute-task-v1.json and anchor-binding-v1.json — every task identity, signature and hash resolves there or is derived with the same method; test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json supplies the submitter test key",
    "consensus": "docs/rfcs/0005-compute-task-commitment-v1.md — RPC represents the object and validates nothing; rules (k)–(s) live in the node",
    "block_fields": "docs/rfcs/0006-chain-identity-authenticated-blocks.md section 3 (BlockHeader.producer and Block.producer_signature, appended) and section 7 (block results gain both, in the 0x hex of rpc_v0.3)"
  },
  "conventions": {
    "json_byte_encoding": "Address and Hash → \"0x\" + 64 lowercase hex; signature → \"0x\" + 128 hex; plain [u8; N] / Vec<u8> (salt, input_commitment, execution_spec, and the receipt's task_id, input_commitment, output_commitment, metadata) → array of numbers 0..=255; u128 / u64 / u8 → JSON number",
    "payload_tagging": "externally tagged: \"None\" is the bare string; the other variants are single-key objects {\"AnchorReceipt\": {…}} and {\"ComputeTask\": {…}}",
    "hex_in_expected": "lowercase, no 0x prefix, as in the protocol fixtures",
    "task_id": "not a wire field of the transaction: derived by the client per RFC 0005 §2.2 (BLAKE3(DOMAIN_TASK || SCALE(task))) and carried on the wire only inside a receipt's task_id array"
  },
  "derivation": {
    "method": "Objects assembled by hand from the serde annotations; the transfer and the minimal task were signed here with an independent Ed25519 over hand-laid SCALE; the canonical and maximal tasks were re-derived and checked byte-for-byte against compute-task-v1.json; the anchor object is the bound-named-executor vector of anchor-binding-v1.json rendered to JSON; transactions_root is an independent BLAKE3 over length-prefixed SCALE transactions.",
    "machine_inputs": "the three protocol fixtures named under authority",
    "version_2": "Derived from test-vectors/rpc/compute-task-rpc-v1.json: for each signed transaction, the test seed was found by reproducing the v1 signature over the v1 signing bytes, then the transaction was signed again over \"mbongo-tx:v2\" || chain_id || fields with an Ed25519 written independently of ed25519-dalek and @noble, and its encoding and BLAKE3 hash recomputed. The block's transactions carry their new signatures, so its transaction hashes and transactions_root were recomputed (BLAKE3 over each encoding prefixed by its u32 little-endian length).",
    "version_3": "Derived from compute-task-rpc-v2.json, which is unchanged: every transaction and payload object is the same. The block object gains header.producer, the dev authority (public key of the public seed BLAKE3(\"mbongo:dev-authority:v1\")), as the last header field, and producer_signature as the last block field: Ed25519 over BLAKE3(\"mbongo-block:v1\" || chain_id || SCALE(header)) for the dev chain, with the S1-2 Ed25519 (the same bytes as OpenSSL) and the S1-5 BLAKE3, the header SCALE laid by hand. RPC represents the block and validates nothing: parent_hash and state_root stay zero."
  },
  "test_key": {
    "warning": "TEST ONLY. NOT A PRODUCTION KEY.",
    "source": "resolved from test-vectors/receipt/receipt-v1.json test_key"
  },
